# cmd.exe REQUIRES CRLF. A batch file saved with bare LF endings parses catastrophically —
# it silently drops the leading character of most lines ("echo" becomes "cho", "call" becomes
# "l") and the script fails in a way that looks like a corrupt install rather than a line-ending
# problem. Pin these so an editor or tool that prefers LF cannot break them again.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise in the repo, let git decide on checkout.
* text=auto
